                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8910e00c-f8d2-301f-af28-fbf7b28c1727",
                        "entry_id": "d23eddf2-de14-38d5-a778-dec48e9ad98d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Erstarrung der Muskulatur eines toten Körpers, die wenige Stunden nach dem Tod eintritt und anhält bis die ersten Verwesungsprozesse beginnen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "99a4299c-3f13-49b6-947d-2575c661cfba",
                                "sense_id": "8910e00c-f8d2-301f-af28-fbf7b28c1727",
                                "text": "Da die Leichenstarre noch nicht eingesetzt hat, kann er noch nicht länger als zwei Stunden tot sein."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31668c7b-e16b-46b9-97fe-dc73e90b87a5",
                                "sense_id": "8910e00c-f8d2-301f-af28-fbf7b28c1727",
                                "text": "„Später erfuhr ich: Beginn und Ende der Leichenstarre sind für Kriminalisten wichtige Anhaltspunkte.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "53d65bbc-886f-42b2-8672-77631e87b540",
                        "source_entry_id": "d23eddf2-de14-38d5-a778-dec48e9ad98d",
                        "source_sense_id": "8910e00c-f8d2-301f-af28-fbf7b28c1727",
                        "source_sense_description": "Versteifung einer Leiche",
                        "target_lang_word": "rigor mortis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rigor mortis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "976d7d38-b580-330c-a43a-ec02b60f6be1",
                                        "entry_id": "15b142c0-ab57-3480-8380-619f60d422ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Temporary stiffness of the body's muscles and joints following death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18ad018f-6649-4af3-8b52-20f163a011ce",
                                                "sense_id": "976d7d38-b580-330c-a43a-ec02b60f6be1",
                                                "text": "Such are the principal phenomena observed during that form of contraction which I conceive to be analogous to the rigor mortis..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ca2aa29-0d9d-44df-bbe9-67feb7befa86",
                                                "sense_id": "976d7d38-b580-330c-a43a-ec02b60f6be1",
                                                "text": "Then we carried in poor Austin from the yard. His muscles were set as hard as a board in the most exaggerated rigor mortis, while the contraction of the fibres had drawn his mouth into a hard sardonic grin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1863eb95-61c8-4bd1-90ff-eb80b46dedd5",
                                                "sense_id": "976d7d38-b580-330c-a43a-ec02b60f6be1",
                                                "text": "[…]an unpublished writer who, for all his ambition and flashes of talent, had not been trained in the rigours (nor rigor mortises, for that matter) of a university education."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9221ed5a-b4a7-4023-a48d-282ee99c6c1d",
                                                "sense_id": "976d7d38-b580-330c-a43a-ec02b60f6be1",
                                                "text": "Its wood can neither be carved nor used for the making of the furniture because of the volatility of those characteristics of the nutrients it has sucked which come from innumerable varieties of rigor mortises."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dc27271-dce9-4be1-9ba7-0c204257f61c",
                                                "sense_id": "976d7d38-b580-330c-a43a-ec02b60f6be1",
                                                "text": "Instead, Tender Buttons destabilizes persistent syntactic arrangements and lexical rigor mortises to assert that “certainly glittering is handsome and convincing,” glittering a radiant process of flux and variance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rigor mortis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                        "entry_id": "7ced09d3-c628-3c86-b3d9-aba79de72d8f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stiffen the muscles and joints with, or as if with, rigor mortis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61d71206-b017-4a3c-8dd0-267b6ccf71ff",
                                                "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                                "text": "As Olive was in the kitchen making some tea I asked what kind of louse the host was. “The kind you like to see laying out on a mortuary slab rigor mortising before the introduction.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2f811ae-4a3d-4008-b214-a31d67b8854b",
                                                "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                                "text": "Hands / Responding to bold brain waves, / Hiding feelings, / Twiddling facts, / Dating destinies, / Doting on things, / Withering in death traps, / Snapping brittle, / Folding stiffly / When movement ceases / And rigor mortises the joints."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12e7e1fc-1c09-4bf4-93df-c68bbace77a9",
                                                "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                                "text": "Fingers were rigor mortised to triggers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78029a26-3cb5-4cee-9156-53ba5ecebca0",
                                                "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                                "text": "Let the old woman point until her finger rigor mortises and she has to bandage it in the daytime and pretend it got caught between the rocks, grinding corn into meal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a088da18-9117-4aed-9f44-efb57280ebd3",
                                                "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                                "text": "Forget rigor mortising, clutter of taxidermy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "808b3973-5d02-4ce6-b124-d6bd89e4147d",
                                                "sense_id": "d2789156-7385-3279-aa82-70506b667ebd",
                                                "text": "At McCray’s, we had to lift Pa off Flash in the folded position he had rigor mortised to."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
